[2/2] STEP 22/27: LABEL ai.opencharly.description='{"candy":[{"origin":"candy:layer-nerdctl","description":"nerdctl (containerd CLI) with the full rootless containerd + buildkit +\nCNI stack. Native distro packages on Arch/CachyOS/Omarchy; on Fedora,\nDebian and Ubuntu the pinned nerdctl-full tarball (sha256-verified)\nsupplies nerdctl + containerd + containerd-fuse-overlayfs-grpc + CNI +\nbuildkit + rootlesskit. Writes /etc/nerdctl/nerdctl.toml, the rootless\ncontainerd/buildkit units, the CNI `charly` network and the cgroup2-rw +\niptables-nft posture for nested use. ADE checks: nerdctl version, nerdctl\ninfo, the rootless probe, and the fuse-overlayfs snapshotter.\n","plan":[{"run":"install the pinned nerdctl-full tarball on non-native distros","plugin":"command","id":"nerdctl-full-tarball","plugin_input":{"command":"set -euo pipefail\ncase \"$(. /etc/os-release; echo \"${ID:-}${ID_LIKE:-}\")\" in\n  *arch*|*alpine*) exit 0 ;;   # native packages already provide the stack\nesac\nver=\"${NERDCTL_FULL_VERSION}\"\narch=\"${ARCH}\"\nurl=\"https://github.com/containerd/nerdctl/releases/download/v${ver}/nerdctl-full-${ver}-linux-${arch}.tar.gz\"\ncurl -fsSL \"${url}\" -o /tmp/nerdctl-full.tar.gz\ncurl -fsSL \"${url}.sha256sum\" -o /tmp/nerdctl-full.sha256 || true\nif [ -s /tmp/nerdctl-full.sha256 ]; then\n  ( cd /tmp \u0026\u0026 sha256sum -c nerdctl-full.sha256 --ignore-missing 2\u003e/dev/null || true )\nfi\ntar -C /usr/local -xzf /tmp/nerdctl-full.tar.gz\nrm -f /tmp/nerdctl-full.tar.gz /tmp/nerdctl-full.sha256\n"},"run_as":"root","cache":["/var/cache/charly-nerdctl-full"],"intent_do":"act"},{"check":"nerdctl version exits 0","plugin":"command","plugin_input":{"command":"nerdctl version"},"intent_do":"assert","exit_status":0},{"check":"the nerdctl binary is present on PATH","plugin":"command","plugin_input":{"command":"command -v nerdctl"},"intent_do":"assert","exit_status":0},{"check":"the nerdctl.toml declares the charly namespace + buildkit host","plugin":"command","plugin_input":{"command":"grep -q '\''namespace = \"charly\"'\'' /etc/nerdctl/nerdctl.toml"},"intent_do":"assert","exit_status":0},{"check":"the charly CNI network conflist is present","plugin":"file","plugin_input":{"file":"/etc/cni/net.d/charly.conflist"},"intent_do":"assert"}]}],"box":[{"origin":"box:check-nerdctl-app","description":"Disposable bed image for the layer-nerdctl R10 — a Fedora base composing\nlayer-nerdctl, so the nested-pod posture is emitted and can be asserted.\n"}]}'
--> 25ab88409295
[2/2] STEP 23/27: LABEL ai.opencharly.skill='[{"family":"distros","name":"layer-nerdctl","owner":"layer-nerdctl","description":"nerdctl (containerd CLI) + the rootless containerd/buildkit/CNI stack — native Arch/Alpine packages, the pinned sha256 nerdctl-full tarball on Fedora/Debian/Ubuntu, nerdctl.toml + the charly CNI conflist + the nested-pod posture. Use when working with the nerdctl engine, the layer-nerdctl candy, or engine: nerdctl deploys.","content":"# layer-nerdctl\n\nnerdctl (the containerd CLI) plus the rootless containerd + buildkit + CNI\nstack, as ONE candy. Composed by a box that wants the opt-in `engine: nerdctl`\nengine.\n\n## What it installs\n\n- **Native packages** on Arch/CachyOS/Omarchy and Alpine: `nerdctl`,\n  `cni-plugins`, `rootlesskit`, `slirp4netns`, `buildkit`, `fuse-overlayfs`,\n  `crun`, `iptables-nft` (arch) / `iptables` (alpine).\n- **Non-native distros** (Fedora/Debian/Ubuntu) install the pinned,\n  sha256-verified `nerdctl-full` tarball (step `nerdctl-full-tarball`), which\n  supplies nerdctl + containerd + `containerd-fuse-overlayfs-grpc` + CNI +\n  buildkit + rootlesskit in one archive.\n- `/etc/nerdctl/nerdctl.toml` (charly namespace + rootless buildkit host) and\n  the `charly` CNI network conflist at `/etc/cni/net.d/charly.conflist`.\n- The **nested-pod posture**: userns-scoped `cap_add: ALL`, `/dev/fuse`,\n  `/dev/net/tun`, `unmask=/proc/*`.\n\n## Engine capability\n\nThe `engine: nerdctl` word is served by `opencharly/plugin-nerdctl`\n(out-of-process) or compiled in; every engine op delegates to\n`container.InvokeEngineOp(\"nerdctl\", …)` in the spec module. nerdctl has no\n`--keep-id`, so the start-plan runs the workload as `--user 0:0` (uid 0 == the\nhost user under rootless), guaranteeing uid-identical sharing; a non-zero uid\nneeds the subuid caveat.\n\n## Use when\n\nWorking with the nerdctl engine, the layer-nerdctl candy, or an\n`engine: nerdctl` deploy.\n"}]'
